# The three internal-only trees ADR-115/Rule 0b keeps OUT of this public-track trunk: session
# briefs, evidence artifacts, and the release toolchain. publish-gate.sh already refuses them at
# push time and stays the wall — this is the belt. Ignoring them matters because Rule 0a's
# "a blocked commit means RE-STAGE EVERYTHING" makes a broad re-`git add` the normal recovery
# move, and an internal tree that reaches a commit is far more work to unwind than one that was
# never stageable. Same lesson as authors.vault.json above, applied to the directories.
ralf/
docs/evidence/
scripts/release/

