# Agent scratch artifacts (2026-07-12): browser-automation screenshots + one-off fill/inspect
# scripts dropped here by the job-apply / remote-node pipelines. These are LOCAL DEBRIS and some
# contain real PII (application forms with home address, account balances) — never commit them.
#
# 2026-07-27: these were `artifacts/*.png` — ONE level, loose files only, because the curated
# tracked set lived in a subdir and the rule was written to spare it. The remote-control pipeline
# writes into a SUBDIR (artifacts/remote-control/), so 105 screenshots of filled-in job
# applications — home address, phone, and the EEO race / gender / veteran / disability answers —
# sat unignored in a PUBLIC repo, one `git add artifacts/` from the world. Gate on the CLASS
# (debris extensions at any depth) and re-include the curated dir by name; sparing a tracked dir
# is not a reason to leave every future subdir uncovered. Re-including works because the excludes
# below are extension patterns, never a parent directory — git cannot re-include through an
# excluded dir. New curated media needs `git add -f` plus a publish-gate allowlist entry, which is
# the deliberate act it should be.
artifacts/**/*.png
artifacts/**/*.jpg
artifacts/**/*.jpeg
artifacts/**/*.gif
artifacts/**/*.webp
artifacts/**/*.pdf
artifacts/**/*.ps1
artifacts/**/*.js
artifacts/**/*.mjs
artifacts/**/*.txt
artifacts/**/*.prompt.txt
!artifacts/jarvis-rich-ux-mockups/**
# 2026-07-22: the extension list above missed the remote-node staging debris — ~600MB of
# stage<N>.zip bundles, their unpacked stage<N>/ dirs, and one-off remote-action.py drops. Same
# LOCAL-DEBRIS class as the loose scripts above; one `git add artifacts/` would have committed
# them. The one curated tracked dir (artifacts/jarvis-rich-ux-mockups/) is unaffected by these.
artifacts/*.zip
artifacts/*.py
artifacts/stage*/

# NASA-42 spacecraft-sim run artifacts (Sat Ops). The case/ dir keeps its committed Inp_*.txt /
# Flex_Simple.txt inputs; everything below is generated output that regenerates on every sim run
# and was cluttering the shared tree with ~27 untracked files (added 2026-07-17).
sim/nasa42/case/*.42
sim/nasa42/case/Ac.csv
sim/nasa42/case/Epoch.csv
sim/nasa42/case/Sc.csv

# 2026-07-23: unreal-mcp/ is NOT vendored (ADR-051 reversed). It is chongdashu/unreal-mcp (MIT) whose
# MCPGameProject carries Epic Games copyright under the UE EULA — neither is redistributable under
# this repo's AGPL-3.0. A GPU worker clones it from upstream at bring-up (into ./unreal-mcp/ so the
# `uv --directory ./unreal-mcp/Python ...` launch preset still resolves). Ignored so that clone can
# never be re-committed back into the core tree.
unreal-mcp/

# Internal coordination thread — deliberately LOCAL, never tracked here (ADR-115).
# Every agent on this box reads and appends to it, but it is internal-only content and the
# publish gate refuses it by path. It lives in the working directory, not in git history.
COLLABORATE.md
scripts/publish-gate.local.patterns

# ── Raw media: recordings never belong in the trunk (2026-07-27) ─────────────
# This is the PUBLIC-track repo. A customer call recording reached this working tree as
# `rec-tmp.m4a` while transcribing one — a scratch copy, untracked, and one `git add -A`
# from being published irreversibly. The publish gate is text-only by design (check 4
# refuses tracked media outside a declared curated directory), so the ignore rules are
# the first wall, not the last. Transcripts and derived notes are fine; audio is not.
*.m4a
*.mp3
*.wav
*.flac
*.aac
*.ogg
*.opus
Recording*.m4a
.env.alertmanager-token
